Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:33:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(frontend): add QR tooltip for paste Display URL

Context:
Issue #73 (C QR ADOPT) requires a small self-contained QR for the
paste URL on the official upload-result UI. The gap is in
UploadedPanel, which is upstream-owned, so this lives on an isolated
patch branch from the pinned upstream SHA.

Expected behavior:
After upload, Display URL shows a QR control. Hover/focus opens a
tooltip encoding that public share URL (including #key when encrypted).
Manage URL is not QR-encoded. Existing copy buttons and URL fields
keep their layout.

Acceptance criteria:
- After a successful upload, a QR control is present on Display URL.
- Hovering it reveals a QR image of the Display URL.
- Exactly one QR control; Manage URL has none.
- Dependency is lean-qr only.

Constraints:
- Generic upstream patch; no Feishu concepts.
- No QR redesign, sharing platform, analytics, or navigation overhaul.
- Do not QR the secret Manage URL.

Validation:
- TDD: RED frontend test failed looking for button "QR code"; GREEN
  after lean-qr tooltip on Display URL.
- Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0
- Frontend tests: 3 files / 26 tests PASS
- Worker tests: 16 files / 114 tests PASS
- lint / typecheck / Prettier PASS
- frontend production build PASS

Docs:
- README.md features list
- frontend/test/index.spec.tsx

Upstream base:
0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6

Patch ID:
